another federal appeals court has ruled  against Donald Trump's Muslim ban this  was already the second attempt at the  travel ban you'll remember that the  first version of the travel ban was  defeated in February when it was  declared unconstitutional by a federal  appeals court because it violated the  Establishment cause Clause of the US  Constitution which guarantees freedom of  the religion the administration signed  this new version of the executive order  on March 6th which has slightly looser  provisions just one week later it was  also declared unconstitutional by a US  District Court in Hawaii on May 25th the  federal appeals court in Richmond  Virginia upheld that decision on June  1st the Trump administration appealed  that decision to the Supreme Court and  yesterday in a separate lawsuit the  travel ban was unanimously ruled  unconstitutional by the US Court of  Appeals for the Ninth Circuit in San  Francisco what's fascinating about these  decisions Pat is that the federal  appeals courts have ruled the travel ban  unconstitutional for different reasons  each time the appeals court in Virginia  upheld the unconstitutionality based on  the Establishment Clause violation  before yesterday all rulings against  both versions of the travel ban cited  different combinations of the  Establishment Clause equal protection  and due process this new decision  yesterday from the san francisco u.s.  appeals court said that by signing the  travel ban Donald Trump exceeded the  National Security decision-making power  granted to the president by Congress  judge judge Derek Watson wrote in the  court's opinion quote the order does not  offer a sufficient justification to  suspend the entry of more than 180  million people on the basis of  nationality national security is not a  talismanic incantation that once invoked  can support any and all exercise of  executive power so federal courts are  coming at this from different sides and  they're finding that in multiple